265. General measurement principle (1) The exposure measure for the leverage ratio shall follow the accounting value, subject to the following: (i) on-balance sheet, non-derivative exposures shall be included in the exposure measure net of specific provisions or accounting valuation adjustments (e.g., accounting credit valuation adjustments, prudent valuation adjustments); and (ii) netting of loans and deposits is not allowed. (2) Unless specified differently below, a bank shall not take account of physical or financial collateral, guarantees or other credit risk mitigation techniques to reduce the exposure measure. (3) A bank’s total exposure measure shall be the sum of the following exposures: (i) on-balance sheet exposures; (ii) derivative exposures;
(iii) securities financing transaction (SFT) exposures; and
(iv) off-balance sheet (OBS) items. The specific treatments for these four main exposure types are defined in paragraphs 266 to 269 below.

