32. As the environment in which banks are operating is quite dynamic, the stress testing framework should be reviewed periodically, both qualitatively and quantitatively, to determine its efficacy and to consider the need for modifying any of the elements. The framework should be subjected to at least annual reviews which shall cover, among others, the following aspects: (i) the effectiveness of the programme in meeting its intended purposes; (ii) integration of the stress testing in the risk management processes;
(iii) realistic levels of stress applied;
(iv) systems implementation; (v) management oversight;
(vi) data quality and MIS;
(vii) documentation;
(viii) business and/or managerial assumptions used; and
(ix) any other assumptions used.

